=== NOTES ===

Accordions (FAQs and services) no longer auto-close - any number can be open at
  once, and the indent is hover-only rather than sticking while open. The auto-close
  handler is gone from site.js entirely; the hover rules are in styles.css.
Contact form is now on all 19 pages, not just the homepage, in each page's #contact
  band under an "Or send a message" divider. The markup is identical everywhere
  except two things: the hidden _subject (so the enquiry email says which page it
  came from) and which <option> carries `selected` (so "How can I help?" arrives
  pre-answered). site.js posts it with fetch and swaps the fields for the thank-you
  line in place; the hidden _next is the no-JavaScript path and lands on thanks.html,
  which says the same thing. thanks.html is noindex and deliberately not in the
  sitemap. Description meta on all 19 pages trimmed to under 160 characters, which
  is roughly where Google truncates.
When adding any new page it needs: unique title/description/canonical (keep the
  description under 160 characters), BreadcrumbList
  + Service + FAQPage JSON-LD (FAQ schema must match visible questions exactly),
  a card in #who-i-help, a footer link, a sitemap.xml entry, an llms.txt entry,
  and a copy of the contact form with its own _subject and selected option.
  Also the nav, which now carries "prices" between services and who I help on all 19
  pages, and links in from wherever the page is relevant. Nothing links to an orphan.
Styles and scripts are shared - styles.css and site.js. Don't inline them again.
Illustrations are one shared SVG sprite, injected by site.js and referenced as
  <svg class="ill ill-mark" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#wr-quill"></use></svg>.
  Colour and line weight come from CSS (.ill and the size classes), never from
  the symbol, so the same drawing works at 17px and at 104px. A new niche page
  wants: a .niche-hero-art after the hero container, a .section-mark above each
  .section-title and above the .cta-band h2, a mark inside the .pain-list h2,
  the .callout and the .related h2, and a .footer-mark above the copyright line.
  New drawings go in the sprite in site.js, not inline.
  Keep every symbol's viewBox origin at 0 0. <use> defaults to x="0" y="0", so a
  symbol starting anywhere else renders offset by that amount and gets clipped.
